<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>
  <!--
    A steam locomotive's boiler (docs/development/vehicle-steam-design.md; figures from docs/development/steam-and-diesel-electric-research.md).
    The fire is lit while the locomotive is drafted with fuel aboard (Vehicle Framework's "engine running"); its fuel is the mod's own
    (wood or chemfuel). Not yet tested in game.

    Sources and labels:
    - Steam pressure is held as a share of the boiler's working pressure. Raising steam from cold took "approximately 3 to 7 hours"
      on a heritage railway (primary: the Great Central Railway's engine-shed page); big engines 6 to 10 hours (secondary, anecdotal),
      and a boiler held hot overnight "only takes a couple of hours of firing in the morning" (secondary). The firing and cooling
      rates are set per loadout to land inside those ranges (authored).
    - Safety valves: at least one opens at or below the working pressure and pressure may never pass 6% above it (primary: US 49 CFR
      230.48 and 230.49), so pressure stops at 1.06 and blowing off wastes water.
    - The crown sheet: covered by water, the firebox plate stays near the water's temperature; uncovered, it heats toward the fire's
      1,500 to 2,500 F and steel has lost about 85% of its strength by 1,600 F (primary: NTSB SIR-96/05, quoting Railway Mechanical
      Engineer, 1943). A fusible plug in the crown melts first (UK pure lead at 327 degrees C; primary: the Heritage Railway
      Association's boiler code HGR-B9008), vents steam onto the fire, and "the locomotive must be taken to a maintenance facility for
      repair" (primary: NTSB). US rules never required plugs (primary: 49 CFR 230.59, via the NTSB). A loadout says whether its
      boiler has one (fusiblePlugFitted). Without one, a dry crown sheet tears and the boiler explodes: the water flashes to steam of
      "perhaps 1500 or 2000 times" its volume, and at only 60 psi each cubic foot of boiler water holds the energy of a pound of black
      powder (primary: NTSB, quoting Railway Mechanical Engineer and G. B. Airy). That happens only with the player's boiler
      explosions setting on (owner, 8 Nov 2026: off by default, with a warning); with it off, every boiler behaves as if plugged.
      The explosion's size here (5.9 cells, 60 blast damage) is authored, far smaller than a real one.
    - The water glass must read at least 3 inches above the crown sheet (primary: 49 CFR 230.51): here the glass reads 0 to 1 and
      the crown is uncovered at 0.1 (authored). The injector keeps the glass near 0.8 from the feed water while there is any; priming
      from too high a level is therefore not modelled.
    - Feed water: the tender or side tanks, refilled at a water stop as a service (Dubs Bad Hygiene's water towers when that mod is
      active, otherwise free; owner, 8 Nov 2026), only the shortfall drawn. Each loadout gives its real capacity in litres and a
      scaled one, a tenth of it, used unless the player turns on realistic feed water (owner, 8 Nov 2026: scaled by default; a
      Dubs water tower holds 8,000 and a huge one 50,000, from the mod's own descriptions).
  -->
  <Phobos.VehicleSystems.PhobosVehicleSystemDef>
    <defName>PhobosVehicleSystem_Boiler</defName>
    <label>boiler</label>
    <description>A steam locomotive's boiler and fire. It takes hours to raise steam from cold; the injector feeds it from the tender or tanks; let the water fall below the firebox crown and the fusible plug melts, venting the boiler, and it needs a new plug before it can steam again.</description>
    <roles>
      <li>Boiler</li>
    </roles>
    <parameters>
      <firingRate>0.4</firingRate>
      <steamUse>0.45</steamUse>
      <coolingRate>0.08</coolingRate>
      <waterUse>3</waterUse>
      <injectorRate>4</injectorRate>
      <feedShare>0.2</feedShare>
      <feedWaterLitres>5000</feedWaterLitres>
      <feedWaterLitresScaled>500</feedWaterLitresScaled>
      <fusiblePlugFitted>1</fusiblePlugFitted>
    </parameters>
    <quantities>
      <li>
        <name>steamPressure</name>
        <description>What drives the engine. It builds while the fire burns and falls as the engine works. It cannot move until steam is raised; too high, and the safety valve blows it off.</description>
        <showOnDashboard>true</showOnDashboard>
        <label>steam pressure</label>
        <unit>Fraction</unit>
        <min>0</min>
        <max>1.06</max>
        <startsAt>Empty</startsAt>
        <stages>
          <li>
            <to>0.5</to>
            <label>raising steam</label>
            <notable>true</notable>
            <effects>
              <li Class="Phobos.VehicleSystems.Effect_RefuseMove">
                <reason>PhobosVehicleSystems_RefuseRaisingSteam</reason>
              </li>
            </effects>
          </li>
          <li>
            <from>1</from>
            <label>blowing off</label>
            <notable>true</notable>
            <effects>
              <li Class="Phobos.VehicleSystems.Effect_Sound">
                <sound>PhobosVehicleSystems_SafetyValve</sound>
              </li>
              <li Class="Phobos.VehicleSystems.Effect_RateQuantity">
                <quantity>boilerWater</quantity>
                <perHour>-0.3</perHour>
              </li>
              <li Class="Phobos.VehicleSystems.Effect_Fleck">
                <fleck>Smoke</fleck>
                <perHour>120</perHour>
                <scale>1.2</scale>
              </li>
            </effects>
          </li>
        </stages>
      </li>
      <li>
        <name>boilerWater</name>
        <description>Water over the firebox. It boils away as the engine works and is topped up from the feed water. Let it fall too low with a fire lit and the boiler can burst.</description>
        <label>water in the glass</label>
        <unit>Fraction</unit>
        <min>0</min>
        <max>1</max>
        <startsAt>Value</startsAt>
        <startValue>0.8</startValue>
        <stages>
          <li>
            <to>0.1</to>
            <label>crown sheet uncovered</label>
            <notable>true</notable>
            <effects>
              <!-- With a plug (or with explosions off): the plug melts and vents the boiler. -->
              <li Class="Phobos.VehicleSystems.Effect_SetQuantity">
                <quantity>fusiblePlug</quantity>
                <value>0</value>
                <when Class="Phobos.VehicleSystems.When_All">
                <conditions>
                  <li Class="Phobos.VehicleSystems.When_EngineRunning" />
                  <li Class="Phobos.VehicleSystems.When_All">
                    <invert>true</invert>
                    <conditions>
                    <li Class="Phobos.VehicleSystems.When_Setting"><setting>boilerExplosions</setting></li>
                    <li Class="Phobos.VehicleSystems.When_ParameterBelow"><parameter>fusiblePlugFitted</parameter><value>0.5</value></li>
                    </conditions>
                  </li>
                </conditions>
              </when>
              </li>
              <li Class="Phobos.VehicleSystems.Effect_Letter">
                <label>PhobosVehicleSystems_LetterPlugMeltedLabel</label>
                <text>PhobosVehicleSystems_LetterPlugMeltedText</text>
                <when Class="Phobos.VehicleSystems.When_All">
                <conditions>
                  <li Class="Phobos.VehicleSystems.When_EngineRunning" />
                  <li Class="Phobos.VehicleSystems.When_All">
                    <invert>true</invert>
                    <conditions>
                    <li Class="Phobos.VehicleSystems.When_Setting"><setting>boilerExplosions</setting></li>
                    <li Class="Phobos.VehicleSystems.When_ParameterBelow"><parameter>fusiblePlugFitted</parameter><value>0.5</value></li>
                    </conditions>
                  </li>
                </conditions>
              </when>
              </li>
              <!-- Without a plug and with explosions on: the crown sheet fails. -->
              <li Class="Phobos.VehicleSystems.Effect_Explosion">
                <radius>5.9</radius>
                <damage>60</damage>
                <breakRole>Boiler</breakRole>
                <when Class="Phobos.VehicleSystems.When_All">
                <conditions>
                  <li Class="Phobos.VehicleSystems.When_EngineRunning" />
                  <li Class="Phobos.VehicleSystems.When_All">
                    <invert>false</invert>
                    <conditions>
                    <li Class="Phobos.VehicleSystems.When_Setting"><setting>boilerExplosions</setting></li>
                    <li Class="Phobos.VehicleSystems.When_ParameterBelow"><parameter>fusiblePlugFitted</parameter><value>0.5</value></li>
                    </conditions>
                  </li>
                </conditions>
              </when>
              </li>
              <li Class="Phobos.VehicleSystems.Effect_Letter">
                <label>PhobosVehicleSystems_LetterBoilerExplodedLabel</label>
                <text>PhobosVehicleSystems_LetterBoilerExplodedText</text>
                <letter>ThreatBig</letter>
                <when Class="Phobos.VehicleSystems.When_All">
                <conditions>
                  <li Class="Phobos.VehicleSystems.When_EngineRunning" />
                  <li Class="Phobos.VehicleSystems.When_All">
                    <invert>false</invert>
                    <conditions>
                    <li Class="Phobos.VehicleSystems.When_Setting"><setting>boilerExplosions</setting></li>
                    <li Class="Phobos.VehicleSystems.When_ParameterBelow"><parameter>fusiblePlugFitted</parameter><value>0.5</value></li>
                    </conditions>
                  </li>
                </conditions>
              </when>
              </li>
              <li Class="Phobos.VehicleSystems.Effect_SetQuantity">
                <quantity>steamPressure</quantity>
                <value>0</value>
                <when Class="Phobos.VehicleSystems.When_EngineRunning" />
              </li>
            </effects>
          </li>
          <li>
            <from>0.1</from>
            <to>0.3</to>
            <label>low water</label>
            <notable>true</notable>
            <effects>
              <li Class="Phobos.VehicleSystems.Effect_Message">
                <message>PhobosVehicleSystems_MsgBoilerWaterLow</message>
                <type>CautionInput</type>
              </li>
            </effects>
          </li>
        </stages>
      </li>
      <li>
        <name>feedWater</name>
        <description>The supply the boiler is topped up from. Refill it before it runs dry.</description>
        <label>feed water</label>
        <unit>Fraction</unit>
        <min>0</min>
        <max>1</max>
        <startsAt>Full</startsAt>
        <stages>
          <li>
            <to>0.15</to>
            <label>nearly dry</label>
            <notable>true</notable>
            <effects>
              <li Class="Phobos.VehicleSystems.Effect_Message">
                <message>PhobosVehicleSystems_MsgFeedWaterLow</message>
                <type>CautionInput</type>
              </li>
            </effects>
          </li>
        </stages>
      </li>
    </quantities>
    <flows>
      <li>
        <!-- The fire, while it is lit and the plug holds. -->
        <name>firing</name>
        <quantity>steamPressure</quantity>
        <kind>Into</kind>
        <factorParameter>firingRate</factorParameter>
        <inputs>
          <li Class="Phobos.VehicleSystems.Input_EngineRunning" />
          <li Class="Phobos.VehicleSystems.Input_PartEfficiency">
            <role>Boiler</role>
          </li>
          <li Class="Phobos.VehicleSystems.Input_Quantity">
            <quantity>fusiblePlug</quantity>
            <curve>
              <points>
                <li>(0.49, 0)</li>
                <li>(0.5, 1)</li>
              </points>
            </curve>
          </li>
        </inputs>
      </li>
      <li>
        <!-- Steam to the cylinders: more the harder it works. -->
        <name>cylinders</name>
        <quantity>steamPressure</quantity>
        <kind>From</kind>
        <factorParameter>steamUse</factorParameter>
        <inputs>
          <li Class="Phobos.VehicleSystems.Input_EngineLoad" />
        </inputs>
      </li>
      <li>
        <!-- A boiler losing its heat to the air: slowly, so a hot one keeps steam for hours. -->
        <name>cooling</name>
        <quantity>steamPressure</quantity>
        <kind>Toward</kind>
        <target Class="Phobos.VehicleSystems.Input_Constant"><value>0</value></target>
        <factorParameter>coolingRate</factorParameter>
      </li>
      <li>
        <name>evaporation</name>
        <quantity>boilerWater</quantity>
        <kind>From</kind>
        <factorParameter>waterUse</factorParameter>
        <inputs>
          <li Class="Phobos.VehicleSystems.Input_EngineLoad" />
        </inputs>
      </li>
      <li>
        <!-- The injector keeps the glass near 0.8 while there is feed water. -->
        <name>injector</name>
        <quantity>boilerWater</quantity>
        <kind>Into</kind>
        <factorParameter>injectorRate</factorParameter>
        <inputs>
          <li Class="Phobos.VehicleSystems.Input_Quantity">
            <quantity>boilerWater</quantity>
            <curve>
              <points>
                <li>(0.7, 1)</li>
                <li>(0.8, 0)</li>
              </points>
            </curve>
          </li>
          <li Class="Phobos.VehicleSystems.Input_Quantity">
            <quantity>feedWater</quantity>
            <curve>
              <points>
                <li>(0, 0)</li>
                <li>(0.01, 1)</li>
              </points>
            </curve>
          </li>
        </inputs>
      </li>
      <li>
        <!-- What the injector takes from the tender or tanks: the boiler's glass is a small share of the feed water. -->
        <name>feed</name>
        <quantity>feedWater</quantity>
        <kind>From</kind>
        <factorParameter>injectorRate</factorParameter>
        <inputs>
          <li Class="Phobos.VehicleSystems.Input_Parameter"><parameter>feedShare</parameter></li>
          <li Class="Phobos.VehicleSystems.Input_Quantity">
            <quantity>boilerWater</quantity>
            <curve>
              <points>
                <li>(0.7, 1)</li>
                <li>(0.8, 0)</li>
              </points>
            </curve>
          </li>
          <li Class="Phobos.VehicleSystems.Input_Quantity">
            <quantity>feedWater</quantity>
            <curve>
              <points>
                <li>(0, 0)</li>
                <li>(0.01, 1)</li>
              </points>
            </curve>
          </li>
        </inputs>
      </li>
    </flows>
    <service>
      <label>a water stop</label>
      <dueQuantity>feedWater</dueQuantity>
      <dueBelow>0.4</dueBelow>
      <restores>
        <li>
          <quantity>feedWater</quantity>
          <value>1</value>
        </li>
      </restores>
      <waterLitresParameter>feedWaterLitres</waterLitresParameter>
      <scaledWaterLitresParameter>feedWaterLitresScaled</scaledWaterLitresParameter>
      <waterForShortfall>true</waterForShortfall>
      <work>300</work>
    </service>
  </Phobos.VehicleSystems.PhobosVehicleSystemDef>

  <!--
    The fusible plug, its own system so a mechanic can fit a new one (a system holds one service). A melted plug stops the fire and
    the locomotive until then. Supplies are gameplay stand-ins: steel for the gunmetal body and its lead core (authored).
  -->
  <Phobos.VehicleSystems.PhobosVehicleSystemDef>
    <defName>PhobosVehicleSystem_FusiblePlug</defName>
    <label>fusible plug</label>
    <description>A lead plug in the firebox crown that melts if the water falls too low, venting the boiler before the crown sheet fails. Once melted, the locomotive cannot steam until a mechanic fits a new one.</description>
    <roles>
      <li>Boiler</li>
    </roles>
    <quantities>
      <li>
        <name>fusiblePlug</name>
        <description>A soft plug in the firebox crown. It melts if the water falls too low. Melted, the engine cannot run until it is replaced.</description>
        <label>fusible plug</label>
        <unit>Plain</unit>
        <min>0</min>
        <max>1</max>
        <startsAt>Full</startsAt>
        <hidden>true</hidden>
        <stages>
          <li>
            <to>0.5</to>
            <label>melted</label>
            <notable>true</notable>
            <effects>
              <li Class="Phobos.VehicleSystems.Effect_RefuseMove">
                <reason>PhobosVehicleSystems_RefusePlugMelted</reason>
              </li>
            </effects>
          </li>
        </stages>
      </li>
    </quantities>
    <service>
      <label>a new fusible plug</label>
      <dueQuantity>fusiblePlug</dueQuantity>
      <dueBelow>0.5</dueBelow>
      <restores>
        <li>
          <quantity>fusiblePlug</quantity>
          <value>1</value>
        </li>
      </restores>
      <supplies>
        <Steel>2</Steel>
      </supplies>
      <work>1200</work>
    </service>
  </Phobos.VehicleSystems.PhobosVehicleSystemDef>
</Defs>
